<title>USA: Rorer cancer drug cleared in seven countries.</title>
<headline>Rorer cancer drug cleared in seven countries.</headline>
<dateline>COLLEGEVILLE, Pa. 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rhone-Poulenc Rorer Inc said on Wednesday it received marketing clearance for its Taxotere cancer drug in seven additional countries.</p>
<p>The drug was cleared for the treatment of advanced or metastatic breast cancer in Colombia, Peru, Ecuador, Egypt, Iceland, Bulgaria and Poland, Rorer said.</p>
<p>Regulatory authorities in Bulgaria, Peru, Ecuador and Egypt also cleared Taxotere for use in the treatment of advanced non-small-cell lung cancer, the company said.  </p>
<p>Rorer, which is majority owned by French chemicals group Rhone-Poulenc SA, said its affiliates in the countries are expected to launch Taxotere in the next few months.</p>
<p>Taxotere has now been cleared in 44 countries, the company said.</p>
<p>--New York Newsdesk, 212-859-1610</p>
